# ── Supabase ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in the real values from your Supabase project:
# https://supabase.com/dashboard/project/_/settings/api
#
# The app detects when these are missing and renders a friendly state instead
# of crashing, so it also works locally without them.
#
# Without them there is no backend: sign-in and booking simply report that the
# deployment is unconfigured (see NEXT_PUBLIC_ALLOW_DEMO below for the demo
# layer that used to kick in automatically).

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key

# ── Optional: demo layer ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A localStorage-backed account system (seeded credentials live in
# `src/libs/auth/demo.ts`) that lets the whole app be reviewed without any
# backend. It stores passwords in plain text, so it is OFF unless the build
# opts in — turn it on locally for reviews, never on a real deployment.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ALLOW_DEMO=1

# ── Optional: real payment gateway (Stripe) ─────────────────────────────────
# The booking flow always goes through a payment step. Without keys it uses the
# built-in test gateway (card 4242 4242 4242 4242). With keys, the payment form
# requests a Stripe Checkout Session from `/api/checkout` and redirects there:
# https://dashboard.stripe.com/test/apikeys
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_xxx
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_xxx